# Synchroteam Middleware — HTTP Requests
# Use this file in JetBrains Rider, IntelliJ HTTP Client, or VS Code REST Client extension.
#
# Prerequisites to run the middleware locally:
# - Configure Synchroteam settings via one of the following:
#   - Environment variables for the middleware process:
#       SYNCHROTEAM_BASE_URL (e.g., https://yourtenant.synchroteam.com)
#       SYNCHROTEAM_API_KEY (if your tenant requires it)
#   - Or set values in Synchroteam/Middleware/appsettings.json under the "Synchroteam" section
# - Run the middleware project (Synchroteam.Middleware)
# - Default ASP.NET Core Kestrel ports are typically 5000 (http) and 5001 (https)

### Variables / Environments
@host = http://localhost:5000

### Health check
GET {{host}}/health
Accept: application/json

### Create or upsert a customer by myId/name (no Id provided => POST)
POST {{host}}/sync-to-st/customer
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "myId": "028257",
  "name": "Jose Martinez",
  "email": "manolo@itia.mx",
  "phone": "+52-55-5964-8139",
  "address": {
    "line1": "Uxmal 77B 301, Santa Cruz Atoyac",
    "city": "Benito Juarez",
    "state": "CDMX",
    "postalCode": "03310",
    "country": "MX"
  }
}

### Update (upsert) existing customer by numeric Id (=> PUT under the hood)
POST {{host}}/sync-to-st/customer
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "id": 42,
  "myId": "cust-123",
  "name": "Acme Corp International",
  "email": "ops@acme.com",
  "phone": "+1-555-0100",
  "address": {
    "line1": "100 New Ave",
    "city": "Gotham",
    "state": "NJ",
    "postalCode": "07001",
    "country": "US"
  }
}

### Negative test: missing both name and myId (should return 400)
POST {{host}}/sync-to-st/customer
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "noid@example.com"
}

